Upstream-Status: To upstream [stale __version__ string in the v2.5.1 tag, not riscv64-specific]

The v2.5.1 tag's CHANGELOG entry ("v2.5.1 4/8/26") is real and distinct from
v2.5.0 ("v2.5.0 3/3/26"), but python/finufft/finufft/__init__.py was never
bumped: it still reads `__version__ = '2.5.0'`. scikit-build-core's
`[tool.scikit-build.metadata.version]` config extracts the wheel's Version
metadata from exactly this string (a regex provider reading finufft/__init__.py,
not the git tag name), so the built wheel's own METADATA declares Version:
2.5.0 even though we checked out and built v2.5.1. Confirmed directly: the
publish job's `ci_scripts/update_doc.py --validate-only` step reads the real
wheel METADATA (the same way it would for any package) and correctly refused
to document a 2.5.0 release under our `- version: 2.5.1` entry, since no such
entry exists - not a bug in our own tooling, which trusts the wheel's own
metadata as ground truth, by design.

Bump the embedded string to match the real tag we build.

diff --git a/python/finufft/finufft/__init__.py b/python/finufft/finufft/__init__.py
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/python/finufft/finufft/__init__.py
+++ b/python/finufft/finufft/__init__.py
@@ -17,4 +17,4 @@
 from finufft._interfaces import nufft2d1,nufft2d2,nufft2d3
 from finufft._interfaces import nufft3d1,nufft3d2,nufft3d3

-__version__ = '2.5.0'
+__version__ = '2.5.1'
